Authors: sis78 Samiyah Syed & joa43 Janine Al-Zahiri


Overview:

    chatd is a multithreaded TCP chat server written in C. It accepts a port number as a command line argument and listens indefinitely for incoming client connections. 
    Each new connection is handled in its own thread, allowing multiple clients to chat simultaneously. 
    The server maintains a shared list of connected users protected by a mutex to prevent data races between threads.
    Once connected, a client must choose a unique screen name via a NAM message before they can interact with the chat room (#all). 
    After joining, clients can send messages to all users or privately to a specific user (MSG), update their status (SET), and query information about other users (WHO). 
    The server validates all incoming messages and responds with appropriate error codes for malformed, illegal, or out-of-range inputs.


Testing Plan:

    We tested the following commands and received the expected outputs (multiple connections at once)
        (numbers are the order in which they were sent in their respective terminals)

       1. 1|NAM|8|Regulus|
           2. 1|SET|16|Getting revenge|
           5. 1|MSG|8|#all|hi|
           8. 1|SET|7|Sighing|
           13. 1|SET|8|Amused|
           14. 1|MSG|8|#all|No|
           15. 1|SET|5|exit|
            
       3. 1|NAM|6|James|
           4. 1|SET|18|Playing quidditch|
           6. 1|MSG|35|Regulus|Private message to Regulus|
           7. 1|SET|20|Pathetically pining|

       9. 1|NAM|7|Sirius|
           10. 1|WHO|5|#all|
           11. 1|SET|9|Enraged|
           12. 1|MSG|11|#all|Stop.|

    We tested the following incorrect commands, and received the expected error codes 
        Name in use (1)
            1|NAM|8|Regulus|
            1|NAM|8|Regulus|

        1|MSG|8|#all|hi
            incorrect formatting, unreadable (0)

        1|MSG|35|Regulus|Private message to Regulus|
            Unknown recipient (2)

        1|NULL|
            illegal character (3)

        1|NAM|49|dfajkhfdakjhsdfkjshdfjkhskjfdhksjdhfkjsdhfsdfsdf|
            Too long (4)
